{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06CZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$q : \\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$1$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$p$", "MATH_0006": "$q$", "MATH_0007": "$q \\circ p$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-composition-formally-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d2bfb0551e8398a86d4ba18146c5984c9b9f89e47f8a52960dfe5faaa1fa194f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fd10076484882d660beb678919f8f5dc51f199e8095afa861a80d247ab95a905", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002>\nbe <MATH_0003>-morphisms of categories fibred in groupoids over <MATH_0004>.\nIf <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> are formally smooth on objects, then so is the composition\n<MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:db20394c42d2472829e4ae2b71ad5c7c96a71ee5f432f4b2e8c1f67ce6f93c84", "unit_id": "tag:06D2:statement"}
{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06CZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U \\subset U'$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$z'$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0005": "$U'$", "MATH_0006": "$x$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0008": "$U$", "MATH_0009": "$\\gamma : q(p(x)) \\to z'|_U$", "MATH_0010": "$q$", "MATH_0011": "$y'$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0013": "$U'$", "MATH_0014": "$\\beta : y'|_U \\to p(x)$", "MATH_0015": "$\\gamma' : q(y') \\to z'$", "MATH_0016": "$p$", "MATH_0017": "$x'$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0019": "$U'$", "MATH_0020": "$\\beta' : x'|_U \\to x$", "MATH_0021": "$\\gamma'' : p(x') \\to y'$", "MATH_0022": "$x'$", "MATH_0023": "$U'$", "MATH_0024": "$$\nq(p(x')) \\xrightarrow{q(\\gamma'')} q(y') \\xrightarrow{\\gamma'} z'\n$$", "MATH_0025": "$\\beta' : x'|_U \\to x$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-formally-smooth}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{equation-formally-smooth}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{equation-formally-smooth}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5ed638deddd7c1e57243a744d8b809be2f7ee11bb101fe4e7bad4459da839c20", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:57e66dfdbd707f3bfff10b5355be81791901c81700670ecc60dd0495c3b0bdee", "source_text": "This is formal. Let <MATH_0001> be a first order thickening\nof affine schemes over <MATH_0002>, let <MATH_0003> be an object of <MATH_0004>\nover <MATH_0005>, let <MATH_0006> be an object of <MATH_0007> over <MATH_0008>,\nand let <MATH_0009> be an isomorphism. As <MATH_0010> is\nformally smooth on objects there exist an object\n<MATH_0011> of <MATH_0012> over <MATH_0013>, an isomorphism\n<MATH_0014>, and an isomorphism <MATH_0015>\nsuch that (<REF_0001>) is commutative. As <MATH_0016> is\nformally smooth on objects there exist an object\n<MATH_0017> of <MATH_0018> over <MATH_0019>, an isomorphism\n<MATH_0020>, and an isomorphism <MATH_0021>\nsuch that (<REF_0002>) is commutative.\nThe solution is to take <MATH_0022> over <MATH_0023> with isomorphism\n<MATH_0024>\nand isomorphism <MATH_0025>. We omit the verification\nthat (<REF_0003>) is commutative.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:34d0bb43295829330133cc81d7d328175e0137c6f8a7f40383cb0ef05980d76c", "unit_id": "tag:06D2:proof"}
{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06CZ", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-lemma-base-change-formally-smooth}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-lemma-descending-property-formally-smooth}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:53e12d3c2c2bc928049156a63da163769c5da75d762207ed6c1f2d270ba354ac", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that the class of formally smooth morphisms of algebraic spaces is\nstable under arbitrary base change and local on the target in the\nfpqc topology, see\nMore on Morphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\nHence condition (2) in the lemma below makes sense.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e4dec2fd9cac1d688a6f0ec310c25ea47f63c2b5d84dfb1f52f4755a37328f0c", "unit_id": "tag:06CZ:prose-0002"}
